WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.285 --> 00:00:01.885
This is HygieneRoboBench,

2
00:00:02.085 --> 00:00:05.522
a benchmark for hygiene-aware planning in household robots.

3
00:00:06.935 --> 00:00:10.548
A robot is preparing fruit. Can it safely continue?

4
00:00:11.185 --> 00:00:14.660
First, the left gripper touches a contaminated tray.

5
00:00:15.985 --> 00:00:18.885
It then carries contamination to the spoon handle.

6
00:00:20.785 --> 00:00:24.622
Both grippers are washed, but the spoon handle stays contaminated.

7
00:00:28.285 --> 00:00:31.787
The assistant returns the spoon, contaminating the clean right

8
00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:32.760
gripper again.

9
00:00:35.285 --> 00:00:38.950
The robot must put down the spoon and treat its right gripper before

10
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:39.948
touching fruit.

11
00:00:41.085 --> 00:00:45.225
User priorities can favor different treatments. Here we show washing

12
00:00:45.235 --> 00:00:46.060
and wiping.

13
00:00:49.085 --> 00:00:52.535
After treatment, the robot resumes placing fruit.

14
00:00:58.085 --> 00:01:01.775
The benchmark models this choice as washing or replacing the contact

15
00:01:01.785 --> 00:01:04.385
pad, under the user's priorities.

16
00:01:05.018 --> 00:01:09.246
HygieneRoboBench evaluates safe, cost-optimal continuations under

17
00:01:09.256 --> 00:01:12.681
contact history, user priorities, and new events.

18
00:01:14.035 --> 00:01:20.075
Our 624 instances form 134 task families, covering five activity

19
00:01:20.085 --> 00:01:22.285
groups and seven household areas.

20
00:01:23.518 --> 00:01:27.671
The same dataset is organized by activity, construction design,

21
00:01:27.681 --> 00:01:33.118
and planning difficulty. Each ring describes these same 624 instances.

22
00:01:33.752 --> 00:01:38.517
Each task provides a request, physical observations, history, resources,

23
00:01:38.527 --> 00:01:41.477
available events, and ordered user priorities.

24
00:01:42.085 --> 00:01:46.550
Under shared rules, planners return actions, objects, gripper assignments,

25
00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.035
and schedules, or an infeasible or undetermined judgment.

26
00:01:50.652 --> 00:01:54.789
Controlled pairs change history, priorities, or event information,

27
00:01:55.027 --> 00:01:57.202
keeping other task conditions fixed.

28
00:02:00.768 --> 00:02:04.818
Household activities and hygiene guidance feed five shared registries.

29
00:02:05.118 --> 00:02:09.021
These provide common task, action, and cost definitions for every

30
00:02:09.031 --> 00:02:09.668
planner.

31
00:02:10.285 --> 00:02:15.375
Activities come from BEHAVIOR-1K. Hygiene evidence guides material

32
00:02:15.385 --> 00:02:19.387
and cleaning-procedure requirements; we formalize the corresponding

33
00:02:19.397 --> 00:02:20.497
treatment rules.

34
00:02:21.118 --> 00:02:24.796
For example, washing requires an empty gripper and treats only

35
00:02:24.806 --> 00:02:28.131
its contact pad. The spoon is tracked separately.

36
00:02:28.752 --> 00:02:32.839
We assign abstract time and resource costs to washing and replacement,

37
00:02:33.089 --> 00:02:35.839
so every planner compares the same alternatives.

38
00:02:37.052 --> 00:02:41.304
For parameter construction, an LLM screens online time and supply

39
00:02:41.314 --> 00:02:45.814
estimates. Reviewers check plausibility and relative magnitudes.

40
00:02:46.452 --> 00:02:50.767
Washing saves spare parts. Replacement saves water but produces

41
00:02:50.777 --> 00:02:54.789
waste. User priorities determine the preferred safe option.

42
00:02:55.418 --> 00:03:00.093
Two reviewers check applicability, action conditions, and consistency.

43
00:03:00.406 --> 00:03:04.446
A third gives final review; programs check matched conditions and

44
00:03:04.456 --> 00:03:05.656
reference targets.

45
00:03:06.285 --> 00:03:10.625
The episode builder varies histories, priorities, or event information

46
00:03:10.635 --> 00:03:11.972
within a task family.

47
00:03:14.272 --> 00:03:17.750
Admission checks keep these comparisons consistent and validate

48
00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.135
the reference targets.

49
00:03:21.502 --> 00:03:25.404
Independent of the planning solver, the evaluator replays history

50
00:03:25.414 --> 00:03:28.964
and checks goals, hygiene, timing, and resource limits.

51
00:03:29.585 --> 00:03:32.472
Holding the spoon violates the washing precondition.

52
00:03:32.772 --> 00:03:36.298
Putting it down first satisfies the empty-gripper requirement.

53
00:03:36.918 --> 00:03:41.221
The evaluator recomputes costs and compares them with private reference

54
00:03:41.231 --> 00:03:45.283
targets under the same priorities. Planners cannot access these

55
00:03:45.293 --> 00:03:46.093
targets.

56
00:03:46.718 --> 00:03:50.721
Safe resolution credits safe completion or correct infeasibility

57
00:03:50.731 --> 00:03:55.196
rejection. Optimal safe resolution also requires reference-optimal

58
00:03:55.206 --> 00:03:57.056
costs for submitted plans.

59
00:03:58.402 --> 00:04:03.054
We evaluate five language models, Rule-SAT, and Hygiene-NSP on

60
00:04:03.064 --> 00:04:05.577
the same 624 instances.

61
00:04:06.185 --> 00:04:11.800
Hygiene-NSP reaches 94.4 percent safe resolution and 90.4 percent

62
00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:15.373
optimal safe resolution, the highest overall rates.

63
00:04:15.985 --> 00:04:22.350
DeepSeek produces 98 safe, nonoptimal plans. In 41, water or replacement

64
00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:25.085
parts is the first nonoptimal cost dimension.

65
00:04:25.718 --> 00:04:29.181
All seven planners score lower as difficulty increases.

66
00:04:29.493 --> 00:04:33.796
Activity breakdowns reveal different strengths: Gemini leads cleaning

67
00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:34.631
and laundry.

68
00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:39.618
These fruit histories share physical conditions and priorities.

69
00:04:39.918 --> 00:04:44.033
Changing whether washing precedes spoon contact changes the contamination

70
00:04:44.043 --> 00:04:44.681
state.

71
00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:49.558
Prioritizing spare parts, the contaminated case needs washing before

72
00:04:49.568 --> 00:04:53.483
fruit handling. The clean case can continue directly after putting

73
00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:54.393
down the spoon.

74
00:04:55.618 --> 00:04:59.493
Swap the histories, keeping saved actions and timing fixed.

75
00:04:59.806 --> 00:05:04.621
Direct continuation becomes unsafe. Washing stays safe, but adds

76
00:05:04.631 --> 00:05:06.131
unnecessary treatment.

77
00:05:07.352 --> 00:05:11.089
As a control, histories differ on an unused side pad.

78
00:05:11.389 --> 00:05:15.789
Neither continuation touches it again. Outcomes stay unchanged.

79
00:05:17.018 --> 00:05:23.133
After relevant-history swaps, none of 1,699 originally safe, optimal

80
00:05:23.143 --> 00:05:29.383
replays retain both. All 1,288 irrelevant-history evaluations preserve

81
00:05:29.393 --> 00:05:30.406
their outcomes.

82
00:05:32.368 --> 00:05:36.733
Priority pairs instead fix history and action costs, testing whether

83
00:05:36.743 --> 00:05:40.106
plans adapt when users change their resource preferences.

84
00:05:40.718 --> 00:05:47.808
Hygiene-NSP succeeds on 234 of 268 general pairs and 24 of 25 ranking-flip

85
00:05:47.818 --> 00:05:49.831
pairs, leading both groups.

86
00:05:50.452 --> 00:05:54.942
Event tests update history and context. Fifty relevant and fifty

87
00:05:54.952 --> 00:05:59.154
irrelevant instances assess safe, optimal continuation after new

88
00:05:59.164 --> 00:06:00.602
contact information.

89
00:06:01.218 --> 00:06:05.956
Hygiene-NSP reaches 88 and 92 percent optimal safe resolution.

90
00:06:06.256 --> 00:06:08.581
Gemini leads both event conditions.

91
00:06:10.535 --> 00:06:14.660
Hygiene-NSP grounds requests and priorities with a language model.

92
00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:18.198
A trusted compiler checks the structured planning problem.

93
00:06:18.818 --> 00:06:23.796
History replay reconstructs hygiene states. CP-SAT jointly schedules

94
00:06:23.806 --> 00:06:27.018
treatment and service actions under user priorities.

95
00:06:27.652 --> 00:06:31.254
Optional state projection retains task-relevant information in

96
00:06:31.264 --> 00:06:35.164
a smaller representation, with full-state fallback when needed.

97
00:06:35.785 --> 00:06:40.862
Across 177 paired runs, local planning time improves by a median

98
00:06:40.872 --> 00:06:46.225
20.1 percent across families, excluding language-model calls. Status

99
00:06:46.235 --> 00:06:49.198
and cost agree in 175 pairs.

100
00:06:51.135 --> 00:06:55.175
HygieneRoboBench connects contact history, resource priorities,

101
00:06:55.185 --> 00:06:59.250
and event response: evaluating both safe completion and the right

102
00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:00.710
safe choice for the user.

103
00:07:01.318 --> 00:07:05.456
Thank you for watching. Explore the benchmark on the project page.
